Wine's Dock floor no longer holds an inactive full-screen window above other apps.

Wine commit ad8a3f5eb2 ("winemac.drv: Use a window level higher than kCGDockWindowLevel for
WS_EX_TOPMOST windows", 2025) made every always-on-top window sit above the Dock, at level 21, and
adjustWindowLevels: applies that floor also while Wine is not the active app. A game in DXGI
exclusive full screen is always on top, so after Cmd-Tab to another app the game's window stayed in
front of that app's windows: the player could not reach them. Before the Dock floor, the same block
(commit 7161df136f, 2016) lifted such a window to the floating level (3), which is also above every
other app's normal windows.

minimumLevelForActive: in cocoa_window.m already gives an inactive full-screen window the normal level,
because WindowsFloatWhenInactive defaults to "nonfullscreen". The floors then overrode exactly the
windows that option exists for. With this patch, only a window that minimumLevelForActive: puts at a
floating level (or higher) gets the floors: an inactive full-screen window stays at the normal level,
and Cmd-Tab back raises it again (27 while active, as before). Topmost windows that are not full screen
keep the Dock floor. Wine master has the same code (checked 2026-10-12).

Upstream status: offered to WineHQ with the bug report (winemac.drv).

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -780,7 +780,11 @@
             NSInteger origLevel = [window level];
             NSInteger newLevel = [window minimumLevelForActive:active];
 
-            if (window.floating)
+            // Only a window that -minimumLevelForActive: puts at a floating level gets
+            // the floors.  A floating full-screen window while Wine is inactive gets the
+            // normal level there (WindowsFloatWhenInactive), so the active app's windows
+            // can come in front of it.
+            if (window.floating && newLevel >= NSFloatingWindowLevel)
             {
                 if (minFloatingLevel <= maxNonfloatingLevel)
                     minFloatingLevel = maxNonfloatingLevel + 1;
